Wizard, neutral, human female.

So, I said, this credit-cloning business, how is it different 
than just dropping the money and hoping the pet will steal it,
like we always used to do? Then I read up on some spoilers and
gave it a try. Well, really a few tries -- I killed a few of
my characters trying it.

However, with a really huge wand store on DLVL 2 and a really 
huge general store on 3, things worked out splendidly, and 
I acquired a magic whistle, some tripe rations, speed boots.

Minetown was a disappointment, with just a small food and 
lighting store. I had to sell my 5 food rations and buy them 
back 30 times to get all the money, and gave up on getting 
Itz's cash because it would be too many keystrokes. Donated 
cross-aligned 20 times, with donations 11 through 19 all wasted.

Back to the altar on DLVL 6 to get some holy water, bless my 
two magic lamps and trade one for SDSM. Down for the luckstone,
petless by now. Sad feeling. It was the lousy new layout 
with dispersed hidden rooms that I don't know well, so I got 
a loadstone instead of a luckstone.

Had to pray. Then, since I had no luckstone, I rubbed my other 
magic lamp and wished for the Heart of Ahriman! Back to the altar
on 6, sac and sac, clovers but no Magicbane, bag of tricks was 
empty, so I wielded 17 daggers and read ?oEW.

Then I'm descending, what a great start! I can cast id and 
magic missile. I have a marker. I don't like Sokoban 
but I'm willing to do it because I need the BoH. And now, 
look, I have nearly everything, the castle WoW would really 
set me up, and descending all those levels hoping to find 
something useful is looking a bit boring. People even ascend 
with stats like AC -21. 

So, when I kill and eat a tengu and feel in control (the very 
first tengu!), I pull a cursed scroll from my bag and go to 
level 99! This was a mistake, I soon realize; the monsters 
here are just a bit tougher than I would like at my current 
stage of development, especially because I lack so many 
intrinsics.

Up the stairs to the Castle, and kill the dragons with my 
17 daggers and a sleep wand. Open the door to the throne room,
"Omigosh I can't do this!" but there's no backing out from 
here, so I stay back a bit and fight. Here's where the big
break happens:

Giants are first to fill the doorway. By the time the last 
giant is gone, the doorway is blocked by half a dozen boulders.
I stand there and use all my spell points with magic missile,
then go back to the dragon lair (where I can rest a few turns
without being interrupted) and wait to recover spell points, 
and repeat. Cleared out the whole mob that way!

In retrospect, how lucky I was that nobody shot at me with
a wand of striking -- they would have broken my fortuitous
boulder fort. 

And, how silly of me not to think of waiting just beyond the 
first trapdoor. True, I would have had to deal with the 
monsters later, but meanwhile I could missile many of them 
and those who went down the trap would at least be spread 
out more, and I'd be stronger when I met them. This would 
have been a faster and more reliable way, though I suppose 
there's danger of the giants plugging all the holes.

